=========================================================================

blogs is distributed logging on the BSV blockchain. A producer appends
signed, numbered batches of log lines to a stream; overlay hosts keep
them; and one small mined anchor per interval commits the interval's
batches, so any host's copy can be proven complete and any auditor can
prove when a line was committed, against block headers it checks itself.

Batches are never mined. Each rides an unmined carrier transaction whose
one input spends a mined funding output, so it verifies by SPV without
paying for block space, and a producer can retract it by spending that
output. Only the anchors are mined. A host that serves a stream is a
replica, not an authority: a reader and an auditor verify everything a
host answers, and a host that edits a batch produces something that
fails the check.

