Interoperability

blogs speaks published standards and holds no private protocol. Any
overlay host that implements BRC-22 and BRC-24 and loads the blogs host
module can keep a stream and answer for it; any reader that can check a
BEEF against block headers can verify what a host answers. A stream can
be delivered by a multicast plane (BRC-148) or submitted to each host
directly, and the records are the same either way.

